{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\( |x + y - 7| + |4x - y + 12| = 0 \\), we need to understand that the sum of two absolute values is zero if and only if each absolute value is zero. Therefore, we need to solve the system of equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y - 7 = 0 \\)\n2. \\( 4x - y + 12 = 0 \\)\n\nLet's solve this system step by step.\n\nFirst, we have the equations:\n\\[ x + y - 7 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 4x - y + 12 = 0 \\]\n\nWe can solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 7 - x \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 7 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 4x - (7 - x) + 12 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 4x - 7 + x + 12 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 5x + 5 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 5x = -5 \\]\n\\[ x = -1 \\]\n\n","prefix_end":609,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,17767,760,87,488,379,481,220,22,91,488,760,19,87,481,379,488,220,16,17,91,284,220,15,1124,701,582,1184,311,3535,429,279,2629,315,1378,10740,2750,374,7168,421,323,1172,421,1817,10740,897,374,7168,13,15277,11,582,1184,311,11625,279,1849,315,37906,1447,16,13,17767,856,488,379,481,220,22,284,220,15,1124,340,17,13,17767,220,19,87,481,379,488,220,16,17,284,220,15,1124,692,10061,594,11625,419,1849,3019,553,3019,382,5338,11,582,614,279,37906,510,78045,856,488,379,481,220,22,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,220,19,87,481,379,488,220,16,17,284,220,15,1124,2533,1654,646,11625,279,1156,23606,369,17767,379,1124,982,78045,379,284,220,22,481,856,1124,2533,5847,11,582,27679,17767,379,284,220,22,481,856,1124,8,1119,279,2086,23606,510,78045,220,19,87,481,320,22,481,856,8,488,220,16,17,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,220,19,87,481,220,22,488,856,488,220,16,17,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,220,20,87,488,220,20,284,220,15,1124,921,78045,220,20,87,284,481,20,1124,921,78045,856,284,481,16,1124,2533,7039,429,582,614,17767,856,284,481,16,1124,701,582,27679,419,897,1182,1119,279,23606,17767,379,284,220,22,481,856,1124,982,78045,379,284,2