33016,-0.00027092601521871984,-0.06196604669094086,-0.0005559567362070084,0.0,-6.6756979322235566e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-4.768370445162873e-07,-1.311301275563892e-06,-1.9073468138230965e-06,-9.536738616588991e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,11457,6716,315,1931,5109,4930,87,11,379,15087,892,67901,279,23606,400,91,87,10,379,12,22,91,10,760,19,87,481,379,10,220,16,17,87803,220,15,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the ordered pair of real numbers $(x, y)$ which satisfies the equation $|x+ y-7|+ |4x - y+ 12|= 0$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"c41a4fa002fb471d3ff0996e53fdf11aad9b7307210333e0ba89f138f5d75189"},"seconds":11.516204118728638,"seed":218437977946483131,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation \\( |x + y - 7| + |4x - y + 12| = 0 \\), we need to understand that the sum of two absolute values is zero if and only if each absolute value is zero. Therefore, we need to solve the system of equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y - 7 = 0 \\)\n2. \\( 4x - y + 12 = 0 \\)\n\nLet's solve this system step by step.\n\nFirst, we have the equations:\n\\[ x + y - 7 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 4x - y + 12 = 0 \\]\n\nWe can solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 7 - x \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 7 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 4x - (7 - x) + 12 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 4x - 7 + x + 12 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 5x + 5 = 0 \\]\n\\[ 5x = -5 \\]\n\\[ x = -1 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( x = -1 \\), we substitute this value back into the equation \\( y = 7 - x \\):\n\\[ y = 7 - (-1) \\]\n\\[ y = 7 + 1 \\]\n\\[ y = 8 \\]\n\nSo, the solution to the system of equations is \\( (x, y) = (-1, 8) \\).\n\nTo verify, we substitute \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( y = 8 \\) back into the original absolute value equations:\n\\[ |x + y - 7| = |-1 + 8 - 7| = |0| = 0 \\]\n\\[ |4x - y + 12| = |4(-1) - 8 + 12| = |-4 - 8 + 12| = |0| = 0 \\]\n\nSince both absolute values are zero, the solution is correct. Therefore, the ordered pair \\((x, y)\\) that satisfies the equation is \\(\\boxed{(-1, 8)}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(-1, 8)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1164"}
